       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks like an error, and it would be unsafe as written.\n\n- **Requested:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for adults is 800 mg per dose and 3,200 mg/day. This order is twice the maximum daily dose, and each single dose is also twice the usual maximum.\n- **Risks:** At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nHere are some options, depending on what you meant:\n1. **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common regimen for inflammatory pain.\n2. **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum.\n3. **Ibuprofen 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours**, for mild to moderate pain.\n4. **Ibuprofen 1600 mg/day**, if you meant a total daily dose. That could be 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me which regimen you want, and add an indication or note if you'd like one. I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that it's intentional and give me the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
